# Representation-model reference — Mammogram (multi-source) + BMI (cascade)
// ⚠ PRE-REDESIGN FORM — pending the concept-model-redesign rule-B + example refresh.
// This file is the authoring-kit's `concept-layer-model` exemplar (authoring-kit/index.ts),
// but it predates the v3 concept model (tmp/representation-model.md): its `source representation`
// posreps are the OLD permissive form (no `value element` / `value type`, which the Todo-2
// `representation-shape` validator now REJECTS), and `Most Recent Mammogram` computes
// `most recent "Mammogram"` over a BOOLEAN — the exact bad example refinement 1 kills (it must be
// `most recent "Mammogram (ImagingStudy)"`, a dateTime-valued concept). It is DEFERRED, not
// migrated, because completing the Claim / ExplanationOfBenefit / DiagnosticReport posreps needs
// CLINICAL value-element decisions (content authoring, not language work). Do NOT treat this as a
// current, valid exemplar. No automated test validates it today. See disc 396.
library "Representation Examples".

// ============ Terminologies (external systems / value sets) ============
terminology "Mammogram VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/screening/ValueSet/mammogram`.

terminology "Mammogram DiagnosticReport VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/screening/ValueSet/mammogram-dr`.

terminology "Height VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/height`.

terminology "Weight VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/weight`.

terminology "Clinical BMI":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/bmi`.

// ============ Mammogram — external source groupings (possible representations only; read-only) ============
concept "Clinical Mammogram":
- source representation: - type is ImagingStudy. - coded from "Mammogram VS".
- source representation: - type is DiagnosticReport. - coded from "Mammogram DiagnosticReport VS".

concept "Administrative Mammogram":
- coded from "Mammogram VS".
- source representation: - type is Claim. 
- source representation: - type is ExplanationOfBenefit.

// ============ Mammogram — locally coded (`code is`, system = the package) + composed ============
concept "Mammogram":
- type is Observation.
- code is `mammogram`.
- defined as ( "Clinical Mammogram" sem-or "Administrative Mammogram" ).

concept "Most Recent Mammogram":
- type is Observation.
- value type is dateTime.
- definition is most recent "Mammogram".

concept "Mammograms In Last Six Months":
- type is Observation.
- value type is integer.
- definition is count of "Mammogram" within last 6 months.

// Two natural user-assertion points (assert at any level, ADR 0001 §8):
//   - assert the EVENT ("Mammogram") → flows to most-recent, count, and up-to-date;
//   - assert the BOOLEAN ("Up To Date On Mammography") → directly answers the screening question.
concept "Up To Date On Mammography":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `up-to-date-on-mammography`.
- definition is "Most Recent Mammogram" within last 27 months.

// ============ BMI cascade — locally coded at every level ============
concept "Height":
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `height`.
- source representation: - coded from "Height VS".

concept "Weight":
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `weight`.
- source representation: - coded from "Weight VS".

concept "BMI":
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `bmi`.
- definition is body mass index of "Weight" and "Height".
- source representation: - coded from "Clinical BMI".

concept "High BMI":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `high-bmi`.
- definition is "BMI" at least 30 'kg/m2'.
